.git
.github
output.log
*.log
# Bare `*.log` matches root-level files only, so the ever-growing logs/ tree needs its own rule.
logs/
**/archive/
README.md
AGENTS.md
CHANGELOG.md
.gitignore
.dockerignore
docs
linux/webserver
out/
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip
# Only Dockerfile.nvidia reads this, through its own windows context; bare `*.zip` would not keep the TensorRT zip out of the root context.
windows/downloads/
*.swp
*.swo
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
**/node_modules/
.cache/
*.so
*.o
*.a
**/target/
**/build/
!linux/scripts/03-media/build/
!linux/scripts/03-media/build/onnxruntime/build/
# Chain scripts live under scripts/build/, which the generic **/build/ exclusion would swallow.
!windows/scripts/build/
**/dist/
.venv/
venv/
*.whl
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

sphinx-kataglyphis-theme/
*.vs
.vs/
*.pdb
*.exp
*.ilk

# Windows CI/template scaffolding — not consumed by any Windows Dockerfile
windows/scripts/rust/
windows/scripts/python/
windows/scripts/certificates/

# DocumANTation builds from its own Dockerfile; no chain Dockerfile COPYs it.
external/

# Untracked scratch helpers (mirrors .gitignore); bare patterns match root level only, where no Dockerfile COPYs from.
.scratch/
*.py
*.sh
*.ps1
*.psm1
*.tmp
*.bak

# The QNN drop dir is bind-mounted into the costliest media RUNs, so a README edit there must not bust them.
linux/qnn-sdk/*.md

# Home Assistant live state: large, secret, and read by no Dockerfile.
linux/homeassistant/config/
